#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=9 nAlgorithms=5;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version dev) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1795777555147'; [Fri Nov 27 12:05:55 CET 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using RazorNet (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.), (Hayamizu et al, 2026 ; M. Hayamizu, others, DH Huson, in preparation).
The original input consisted of 6 taxa and 6 DNA sequences of length 677.
The Razor Haplo Net method (Hayamizu et al, 2026) was used (default options) so as to obtain 14 nodes and 15 edges.
The Shave Filter method was used (default options, except Target=None) so as to obtain 14 nodes and 15 edges.

References:
Hayamizu et al, 2026: M. Hayamizu, others, DH Huson, in preparation
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
]

BEGIN TAXA;
TITLE 'Input Taxa';
DIMENSIONS ntax=6;
TAXLABELS
	[1] 'A.andrenof'
	[2] 'A.mellifer'
	[3] 'A.dorsata'
	[4] 'A.cerana'
	[5] 'A.florea'
	[6] 'A.koschev'
;
[DISPLAYLABELS;]
[TAXINFO;]
END; [TAXA]

BEGIN ALGORITHM;
TITLE 'Taxa Filter';
NAME 'Taxa Filter';
OPTIONS
;
END; [ALGORITHM]

BEGIN TAXA;
TITLE 'Working Taxa';
LINK ALGORITHM = 'Taxa Filter';
DIMENSIONS ntax=6;
TAXLABELS
	[1] 'A.andrenof'
	[2] 'A.mellifer'
	[3] 'A.dorsata'
	[4] 'A.cerana'
